Department:
Strategic Advisory Group

Pembina Pipeline Corporation is a dynamic energy transportation and midstream provider, serving customers for more than 70 years. Chances are, we do more than you think. We own pipelines that transport hydrocarbon liquids and natural gas products produced primarily in Western Canada. We also own gathering and processing facilities and an oil and natural gas liquids infrastructure and logistics business. Our operations along the hydrocarbon value chain allow us to offer a full state of midstream and marketing services to our customers in the energy industry.

We are an organization that cares not only about results, but how those results are achieved. Our organization is grounded in the values of Safe, Trustworthy, Respectful, Collaborative and Entrepreneurial Pembina has a diverse and inclusive working environment that provides employees with a positive and engaging work experience where they are recognized and empowered. Learn more about our values and strategy.

We value the safety of our communities, customers, contractors and employees, and believe that all incidents are preventable. Compliance with all policies, procedures and regulations is a requirement, and our Life Saving Rules are basic rules. Employees embed physical, psychological, and cyber safety into all work practices while taking personal accountability to maintain compliance, support audit readiness, proactively identify risks, and protect our people, assets, and data. Working for Pembina means working safely.

Overview:

Pembina’s Pipeline’s Legal, People and Corporate Division is actively hiring a Director of HR Strategic Business Partnering in the Calgary office. Reporting to the Vice President of Human Resources, the Director will be an influential member of the HR Leadership team, helping shape people strategy, provide direction and advance organizational priorities across Pembina.

The Director is a Senior HR leader responsible for strengthening the connection between Pembina’s business strategy and its people strategy. Leading Strategic Business Partnering and Workforce Planning & Talent Acquisition, the Director helps leaders look ahead, anticipate workforce needs and build the talent and capabilities required to deliver Pembina’s future. Leading a team of managers, the Director works across Human Resources to shape priorities, strengthen how HR partners with the business and drive greater impact across the organization.

Pembina’s Human Resources plays a key role in enabling the company’s 3Cs Strategy through its people: strengthening leadership, talent and organizational capability to support continued growth and long-term success. The department plays a lead role in shaping a high-performing, accountable and inclusive culture by providing leadership, direction and influence across the organization. It is accountable for building leadership capability, strengthening talent programs and creating an environment where people are empowered to contribute, develop and succeed.

Responsibilities:

Serve as a key member of the HSU Senior Leadership team, working with fellow Directors to collectively own the whole of the people function, shaping People Strategy, HR priorities, and governance, and leading enterprise initiatives that extend beyond the Strategic Business Partnering portfolio;
Act as a trusted advisor to executive and senior business leaders, providing strategic counsel on workforce, talent, leadership, organization, and employee relations matters, and translating business strategy into clear people priorities and outcomes;
Set the direction and standards for strategic business partnering across Pembina, ensuring HR partners are embedded in the business, anticipate needs, and deliver integrated people solutions that drive business performance;
Advance Pembina’s strategic workforce planning capability, building a consistent, forward-looking approach that integrates with business and financial planning. Enable leaders to anticipate future capacity, capability, critical role and workforce cost needs, while leveraging AI, automation and emerging technologies to rethink how work is delivered and determine the optimal mix of people, technology and external resources;
Build and lead a high-performing leadership team of managers spanning Strategic Business Partnering and Workforce Planning & Talent Acquisition, setting clear direction and accountabilities, developing leadership bench strength, and role modelling inclusive leadership, accountability, and a strong learner mindset;
Provide HR leadership for major projects, joint ventures, and significant business change, guiding organization design, workforce structure, and change strategies that enable business objectives;
Partner with fellow HSU Directors across Operations & Total Rewards and Leadership, Talent & Learning to integrate programs, share accountability for enterprise people outcomes, and ensure talent, succession, performance, leadership, and engagement programs are delivered consistently with measurable business impact;
Use workforce, labour market, and business insights, in partnership with HR Operations, to inform leadership decisions, anticipate risk, and measure the impact of people investments;
Provide strategic oversight of employee and labour relations within the business, supported by specialist expertise on the team, to foster a constructive workplace, manage risk, and ensure consistency and compliance;
Advance equity, diversity and inclusion across the organization by strengthening inclusive workforce planning and talent practices, influencing leadership decisions and behaviours, and identifying and removing systemic barriers to equitable participation, development and career progression; and
Champion Pembina’s Zero by Choice safety culture and Life Saving Rules by embedding physical, psychological, and cyber safety into all HR practices. Ensure compliance while empowering employees to speak up, remain vigilant to risks, and actively protect our people, assets, and data.

Qualifications:

Progressive senior HR leadership experience in strategic business partnering, including leading leaders, with a track record as a trusted advisor to executive teams in complex, operational, or asset-intensive organizations;
Experience leading strategic workforce planning that translates business strategy into future capacity, capability, and cost needs, including guiding leaders on the right blend of employees, contractors, and AI and automation, and leading the role redesign, reskilling, and change required to realize it;
Experience leading or providing strategic oversight of talent acquisition, with a strong understanding of talent markets, sourcing strategies, and employer brand;
Working knowledge of employee and labour relations, with sound judgment on when to engage specialist expertise;
Embodies Pembina leadership capabilities: models safety, enables results, develops people, champions inclusion, demonstrates learning agility, and leads through change;
Proven ability to lead through transformation, guiding organization design, change, and major projects, joint ventures, or partnerships while building organizational capability and resilience;
Strong business and financial acumen, with the ability to connect people priorities to business performance and influence decisions at the executive level;
Data-driven leader with a proven ability to use workforce analytics, metrics, and insights to inform decisions, anticipate risk, and drive accountability;
Effective communicator who engages and influences at all levels, fostering trust, clarity, and alignment across the organization;
Enterprise-minded leader who builds strong, collaborative relationships with peers and inspires high-performing teams through inclusive leadership, psychological safety, and positive influence;
Champions equity, diversity, and inclusion through forward-thinking practices embedded in leadership, talent strategies, and workplace culture; and
Bachelor’s degree in Human Resources, Business, or a related field. An HR designation (CPHR) or advanced degree is preferred.

The successful candidate must be legally able to work in the country of the position. The final candidate will be required to undergo Pre-Employment Background Checks including a Criminal Record Check.

This position is scheduled to be posted until end of day: 12/15/2026. In rare circumstances, a position may be posted for less time if there has been significant interest in the role.

Our expectations are high, and our total rewards package reflects this.

Diverse perspectives, backgrounds, and experiences contribute to our collective success and enrich our workplace culture. We encourage applications from individuals of all backgrounds and experiences. If you're contacted to set up an interview and you require accessibility accommodations, please let your Talent Acquisition Advisor know at that time.

No agency calls please.

